      "type": "paragraph",
      "num": "§ 01",
      "original": "It was disappointing not to have brought back in the evening some important statement, some authentic fact. Women are poorer than men because—this or that. Perhaps now it would be better to give up seeking for the truth, and receiving on one's head an avalanche of opinion hot as lava, discoloured as dish-water. It would be better to draw the curtains; to shut out distractions; to light the lamp; to narrow the enquiry and to ask the historian, who records not opinions but facts, to describe under what conditions women lived, not throughout the ages, but in England, say in the time of Elizabeth.",
      "zh": "到了傍晚也没能带回什么重要的论断、什么确凿的事实，这着实令人失望。女人之所以比男人贫穷，是因为——如此这般。也许现在倒不如放弃追寻真理，免得再让滚烫如熔岩、浑浊如洗碗水一般的意见雪崩劈头盖脸砸在自己头上。倒不如拉上窗帘，隔绝纷扰，点亮台灯，把探寻的范围收窄，去请教那不录意见而只记事实的历史学家，请他描述一下女人在怎样的条件下生活——不必纵贯千古，只说在英格兰，比方说在伊丽莎白时代。"
